{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/68557-prometheans-from-an-informed-outsider-s-point-of-view","id":68557,"title":"Prometheans from an informed outsider's point of view","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-09T11:35:25-08:00","id":68557,"title":"Prometheans from an informed outsider's point of view","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> So I was hoping to feature the occasional Promethean in a game I'm running sooner or later, but have zero familiarity and none of the books. I didn't want to have to retcon anything if a later player wanted to play one of them or get more involved. I'm shooting for a persistent setting (centralized on Huntsville, Alabama, if that makes any difference), and wanted to do them right.<br /> <br /> So what I'm asking for, could someone give me an overview of what kinds of groups there are, what Prometheans can *do*, and why/when they do it. I'd like to involve more groups than just the &quot;good guys&quot; (if there are any), I don't want to limit myself to the stereotypically &quot;Player&quot; groups or &quot;Enemy&quot; groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T13:44:49-08:00","id":68624,"title":"","content":"Here are the basics:<br /> <br /> Prometheans are reanimated corpses, imbued with a full human consciousness, but with a spark of the Divine Fire (the one stolen by Prometheus for the benefit of humanity) in place of a soul. As such, they are powerfully strong and resilient, and can heal by plugging into a current of electricity, but they are born as &quot;damaged goods&quot;, and spend their existence trying to earn the comfort of a soul, and the transformation of Mortality.<br /> <br /> Beyond their native Superlative Constitution (allows them to ignore all but aggravated damage penalties, and to come back once from death), they also possess Transhuman Potential (can increase any attribute by spending Pyros, their fuel stat). They are welcome nowhere; despite their ruse of humanity, they inflict Disquiet on everyone, turning them into mild obsessives and then into a raging mob, and they taint the land around them should they rest for any length of time. Worst of all, they are prone to Torment, in which they finally give into their frustrations, with the full force of their gifts and Transmutations, which leaves ruin in their wake.<br /> <br /> Prometheans attempt to find the &quot;New Dawn&quot; of humanity by pursuing Refinements, which are the source of their Transmutations, their powers. Aurum, or Gold, is the Refinement of Humanity, and grants gifts of Mesmerism and Deception. Cuprum, or Copper, is the Refinement of Self, and grants the Transmutations of Sensorium and Metamorphosis. Ferrum, or Iron, is the Refinement of Body, and grants Corporeum (transformation of function and refinement of human abilities, compared to the shapechanging of Metamorphosis) and Vitality (feats of monstrous strength). Mercurius, or Mercury, is the Refinement of Pyros (the Divine Flame), and grants Alchemicus (material power), and Vulcanus (pyrokinesis and Pyros manipulations). Finally, there is Stannum, or Tin, the Refinement of Torment, and grants Electrification and Disquietism (manipulating and defending against Disquietism). Each has its own philosophies and rituals, but these are practices, not social groups.<br /> <br /> In fact, the largest social group you'll see is a throng, which is just a handful of the Created bound for mutual support. Some of these might be alchemically bonded, which allows them to transfer Pyros and maintain some mystical awareness of one another. But even these are fractious, as Torment builds and Wastelands warp in strange ways due to imbalances among the members' humours. More than five in one spot means something is very likely up.<br /> <br /> Each Promethean descends from a primogenitor, the first of their Lineage. Frankenstein is the youngest of these, fierce and wrathful, and possessed of tremendous strength, driven by Bile, a humour related to fire. Before them came the Galateids, paragons of human beauty, possessed of the Divine Breath, but debased by their soulessness and slavery to the Sanguine humour. The Tammuz, remembered as Golems, born into slavery and forever fighting its oblivion, as resilient as the earth they rise from, and burdened with the Melancholic humour, Black Bile. There are the Ulgan, torn apart by spirits and ghosts, cursed to see beyond the mortal world, and intuitive by way of the Ectoplasmic humour that governs them. Finally, and first are the Nepri, the Osirans, cold and regal as the pharoahs who underwent the same funereal rituals but could not rise as they do, maimed like their god-king, and blinded by their Phlegmatic humour.<br /> <br /> There may be other Lineages, like the rumored Nuclear Promethean, or other Refinements, like that of the Hundred-Handed Centimani, who cherish monsters and aspire to be them. There are surely Pandorans, true monsters who live only in the warmth of the Azoth, the fire that animates the Prometheans. They hunger for the flame and the flesh that contains it, but they are not truly living, and revert to forms of stone and wood when the Pyros escapes them. There are also the Qashmallim, angels of the Pyros, who manipulate mortals and the misbegotten alike, sowing inspiration and chaos alike, to some invisible end, if there is an end. But the greatest enemy of the Promethean is humanity itself, ignorant and spiteful, and beautiful beyond words.<br /> <br /> Every Promethean is on a pilgrimage to join that teeming, seething mass. They may refuse it, lurk in the wastelands of the world, but Prometheans feel a need to be with humans, and only death or the New Dawn will ever sate that need. So they hunt hidden knowledge, or the tracks of those who have gone before. They experiment with Transmutations, to understand the powers that govern them, the Azoth, and the promise of Mortality. They stumble across real, true understanding of the human condition, and accrue Vitriol, an alchemical precursor to the transformation. And, in the end, they may even finally succeed, because Mortality is no false promise, but a real one hidden behind more heartache and disappointment than any one should ever have to stand. And, if the supplicant is truly fortunate, or truly cursed, she might even carry the knowledge into her new life, Redeemed, and truly ready to appreciate the fruits of her labor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:02:43-07:00","id":87951,"title":"","content":"Just about the only thing you missed (and even this is implied) is that virtually every Promethean is made by another Promethean. The only real exceptions were the progenitors of each Lineage, who were made by mortals known as demiurges; and with the possible exception of Frankenstein\u2019s monster, all of them are dead and gone by now. These days, the only beings capable of making a new Frankenstein\u2019s monster are other Frankensteins; the only ones capable of making a new Ulgan are existing Ulgans; and so on. This is why the groupings are known as Lineages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T11:17:23-07:00","id":88955,"title":"","content":"Considering the effects of disquiet, specially on groups (4-5 prometheans), how playable is really the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T11:23:07-07:00","id":88957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/68557-prometheans-from-an-informed-outsider-s-point-of-view?p=87951#post87951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just about the only thing you missed (and even this is implied) is that virtually every Promethean is made by another Promethean. The only real exceptions were the progenitors of each Lineage, who were made by mortals known as demiurges; and with the possible exception of Frankenstein\u2019s monster, all of them are dead and gone by now. These days, the only beings capable of making a new Frankenstein\u2019s monster are other Frankensteins; the only ones capable of making a new Ulgan are existing Ulgans; and so on. This is why the groupings are known as Lineages.</div> </div> </div> </div>But aren't the books often mentioning later day demiurges, indicating that like vampires the Prometheans may have multiple first generation Prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T13:28:24-07:00","id":89009,"title":"","content":"Yes. New demiurges can pop up at any time, and it also mentions that it's possible for a demiurge to create members of an existing lineage. So someone might find Victor Frankenstein's secret diary and manage to recreate the effort, or someone could dig up some ancient manuscripts and create a Tammuz, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, since Prometheans are obscenely rare to begin with, and demiurges rarer than that, it is certainly reasonable to say most are made by other prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:47:11-07:00","id":89141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/68557-prometheans-from-an-informed-outsider-s-point-of-view?p=88957#post88957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But aren't the books often mentioning later day demiurges, indicating that like vampires the Prometheans may have multiple first generation Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few vague references to demiurges prior to the setting\u2019s last book; but the default assumption of the game is that you\u2019ll be playing a Promethean who was created by another Promethean, and that like creates like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}